A macro-rendered date-like value is written single-quoted so it reloads as the
string it was, not a parsed date.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
---

Body.
-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  core.macros.date: "1970-01-02"
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md completed="{{ macro('core.macros.date') }}"
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 ---
 title: Probe plan
+completed: '1970-01-02'
 ---
 
 Body.
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: completed=1970-01-02
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
completed: '1970-01-02'
---

Body.
-- exit --
0
